==============================================================================================
GENERAL RESPONSE LEMMA:  Delta<A> = (theta/2) Tr( i[rho,A] G ) + O(theta^2)
==============================================================================================
  theta = 0.02. Random Hermitian A and G, random pure rho, no structure imposed.

     d         exact     1st order      |diff|  |diff|/theta^2
  ------------------------------------------------------------
     2    0.00320572    0.00323083    2.51e-05           0.063
     4    0.01690097    0.01675881    1.42e-04           0.355
     8   -0.01993892   -0.02002997    9.11e-05           0.228
    16   -0.05627098   -0.05677244    5.01e-04           1.254
  The last column is bounded, so the difference is genuinely O(theta^2).

