  'sym' is |lo+hi|: the interval is symmetric when spec(G) is.
  'sat' columns are the distance from the constructed optimum to each edge.

==============================================================================================
INSTANCE 2: the VQE gradient is the same expression
==============================================================================================
  A real circuit: psi(t) = W exp(-i t G/2) V|0>, energy <psi|H|psi>.
  Compared: (a) parameter-shift gradient, computed independently;
            (b) the LEMMA with A = H_eff = W^dag H W, rho = |phi><phi|.

     d     param-shift           lemma      |diff|
  ------------------------------------------------
     4   -0.0000000000    0.0000000000    1.67e-16
     8    1.5155789025    1.5155789025    4.44e-16
    16   -0.9616033814   -0.9616033814    3.33e-16

  Agreement here means the variational gradient IS the general response
  with A = H_eff, so the zero-gradient rule is a corollary of the interval
  theorem rather than a separate observation that happens to look similar.
  In particular [G, H_eff] = 0 gives M commuting with nothing to pair
  against, Tr(M G) = 0, and the gradient vanishes identically.
